From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer patch: on AMD, DMB ISH and STLR fence with LOCK NOTL of a private word, not MFENCE

Both translators lowered every full DMB/DSB and the store-load fence after STLR to MFENCE. MFENCE is dispatch-serializing on AMD Zen:
14.5 ns per fence on a Ryzen 5 5600 against ~1.8 ns for a locked RMW (microbenchmark, 2026-11-19). PGR's render thread was CPU-bound
in menus (94% running, UnityMain waiting on it 86%), and half of its samples sat on 3-byte pairs in two heavy regions of libunity.so
built from DMB ISH/LDAR/LDAXR/STLXR loops (Unity's lock-free queues).
On an AMD host (host_platform::kIsAuthenticAMD), EmitFullFence (lite: lite_translator_integer_ctrl.inc; heavy: HeavyOptimizerFrontend)
emits LOCK NOTL of the new ThreadState::barrier_scratch for DMB ISH and STLR: a locked RMW orders earlier stores before later loads
like MFENCE for ordinary memory; NOT leaves EFLAGS alone and needs no register. DSB, DMB of other scopes and every fence on other
hosts keep MFENCE; store-only DMB and LDAR stay fence-free. The decoder tells DataMemoryBarrier whether the barrier is DMB ISH.
From a parallel patch on this PC (/tmp/apklayer-cpu.yRiM1V, "use a locked fence for DMB ISH on AMD": the encoding, the scratch word,
the decoder flag, the AMD and ISH conditions) with STLR added. Test: lite_translate_region_exec_tests StoreLoadBarrierEmitsMfence.
Module libberberis_arm64.

